  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who owns the experiment?",
      "items": [
        "Harness² owns the native seq,k=2 recursion. Our adapters supply a restricted portfolio substrate and accounted proposer.",
        "Our workflow owns paired fixed-versus-adaptive execution, frozen inputs, reviews, accounting and reports.",
        "The fixed arm generates twelve complete portfolios and chooses one blindly; the adaptive arm retains both checkpoints and its selected alias."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Models are different jobs",
      "items": [
        "The agent runner is currently OpenCode; the author and blind selector model is currently Opus 5. These are separate roles and components.",
        "Sonnet 5.5 plans, generates ten answers and reorders them inside each portfolio rollout.",
        "GPT-5.6-luna groups answers; Opus 5 judges quality. Evaluation roles are separate from the Opus author/selector role."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The score-blind boundary",
      "items": [
        "Grouping, quality judgments and grader text do not enter solver, author, reflector or selector context.",
        "The workflow seals both arms before evaluator calls. No evaluation feedback edge returns to the recursive loop.",
        "Every actual provider call passes the same owned admission/accounting and transport boundary; the runner only sees its local proxy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Evidence and visibility",
      "items": [
        "Source/runtime/study identities, immutable harness/output artifacts and intent/result journals support saved replay and explicit unknown liabilities.",
        "Inspect imports a read-only projection in a separate keyless, network-none image. It displays evidence; it does not execute this experiment or manage provider spending.",
        "The static viewer is a visibility surface. No Inspect provider bridge feeds the running loop."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Modularity today",
      "items": [
        "Harness² is pinned at 1cfe254e…; NoveltyBench v1.1 is pinned at 64a23be6…. Replacements require compatibility checks.",
        "The diagram names generic runner and model roles with current choices. It does not imply every replacement already works.",
        "Current operator access is the CLI plus Windows launcher. An MCP server and universal plugin runtime are not implemented."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope of this map",
      "items": [
        "This describes offline-accepted continuation source 029657ee… / 177 inputs. Fresh masked keys are pending; the three-pair continuation has not started.",
        "Citations resolve published source b5a56b68…. Offline acceptance establishes engineering readiness, not scientific completion or a positive experiment result.",
        "The completed first pair is imported through a verified certificate with its original generation and assessment identities. The new accounting state covers the three remaining pairs only.",
        "This is an architecture map, not a claim of general scientific improvement or held-out success."
      ]
    }
  ]
